        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "2c32b29e-9aea-3aa2-a5bd-620855b4efa0",
                "word": "témérairement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fd0508f1-4de4-36b3-9fd3-4b3a4c74ce19",
                        "entry_id": "2c32b29e-9aea-3aa2-a5bd-620855b4efa0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière téméraire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9c014e4-bebc-41cf-a021-addd4e334c7d",
                                "sense_id": "fd0508f1-4de4-36b3-9fd3-4b3a4c74ce19",
                                "text": "Se jeter témérairement dans le péril."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce7901ff-3b0b-494c-a925-400d8fb12a3b",
                                "sense_id": "fd0508f1-4de4-36b3-9fd3-4b3a4c74ce19",
                                "text": "C’est, en vérité, pour des gens qui ne parlent que de l’Écriture, se jouer trop témérairement de ses oracles ; et si l’on n’a rien de plus précis pour expliquer les prophéties, il vaudroit mieux en adorer l’obscurité sainte, et respecter l’avenir que Dieu a mis en sa puissance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1df3ec3-a8d5-4bb7-b3a6-1a77303903e4",
                                "sense_id": "fd0508f1-4de4-36b3-9fd3-4b3a4c74ce19",
                                "text": "Je crains de me flatter trop témérairement,"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b83fd0b0-552f-3576-a8a2-61665e00ba90",
                        "entry_id": "2c32b29e-9aea-3aa2-a5bd-620855b4efa0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Au hasard, inconsidérément."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1275d36b-76a2-4b2d-9bb5-507c0818b59e",
                                "sense_id": "b83fd0b0-552f-3576-a8a2-61665e00ba90",
                                "text": "Comme, le plus souvent, ceux qui savent le moins,\nSont témérairement et juges et témoins."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5bd2e434-89aa-4482-bcf8-64914a81ab66",
                                "sense_id": "b83fd0b0-552f-3576-a8a2-61665e00ba90",
                                "text": "Car la raison a été obligée de céder, et la plus sage prend pour ses principes ceux que l’imagination des hommes a témérairement introduits en chaque lieu."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd0d4cb2-305a-459d-a1ce-dbb40ac33d2b",
                                "sense_id": "b83fd0b0-552f-3576-a8a2-61665e00ba90",
                                "text": "Comme il [Édouard IV] était d’une conſtitution très robuste, on soupçonna son frére Richard, Duc de Gloceſter, d’avoir avancé ses jours par le poison. Ce n’était pas juger témérairement du Duc de Glocester. Ce Prince était un monstre né pour commettre de sang-froid tous les crimes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "741a0157-38fc-3278-820f-b1d75f0baf20",
                        "entry_id": "2c32b29e-9aea-3aa2-a5bd-620855b4efa0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Contre droit et raison."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Justice"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6622e4cd-02bd-4a3a-95dc-21a6399c3959",
                                "sense_id": "741a0157-38fc-3278-820f-b1d75f0baf20",
                                "text": "Pour avoir méchamment et témérairement avancé : Se disait quelquefois dans des arrêts qui condamnaient à une amende honorable."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "05f7009b-7e64-4d6f-be4f-935afc197ffb",
                        "source_entry_id": "2c32b29e-9aea-3aa2-a5bd-620855b4efa0",
                        "target_lang_word": "daringly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "daringly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4bb9154-0c77-3869-bd1f-85c3bd1e16a5",
                                        "entry_id": "69c9b57e-85d7-3665-af90-fa2ab5f0e960",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a daring manner"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17be22bd-d819-4028-9391-9812727d4008",
                                                "sense_id": "c4bb9154-0c77-3869-bd1f-85c3bd1e16a5",
                                                "text": "“Here, waiter,” cried the Johnnie who had dejeunered daringly at 12, “take this bill to the manager and tell him it’s an imposition. Why, you’ve charged more for one poached egg on toast than for an entire portion of those eggs that you scramble.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc71c607-4840-4b5f-bf6d-c4133fdea58f",
                                                "sense_id": "c4bb9154-0c77-3869-bd1f-85c3bd1e16a5",
                                                "text": "The corridor stinks of sweat and cigarette smoke, and I daringly open the window a little. The freshest air floats in, smelling of sappy grasses, the delicate pollens of wild flowers, the resins of the pine forests; hinting at the chill blue scent of distant snows."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c28df90f-8057-4208-b7eb-53e3f3ed71b3",
                        "source_entry_id": "2c32b29e-9aea-3aa2-a5bd-620855b4efa0",
                        "target_lang_word": "foolhardily",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "foolhardily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "faa82910-b378-334e-bf45-1e23ab6b8139",
                                        "entry_id": "8152f0d1-2bae-36ab-8dd3-6beb903b52e8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a foolhardy manner"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b02c4be3-ceb4-4b67-b269-57c4f93d2b0d",
                        "source_entry_id": "2c32b29e-9aea-3aa2-a5bd-620855b4efa0",
                        "target_lang_word": "rashly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rashly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "76026db0-b58a-3271-ac62-81e806ed917d",
                                        "entry_id": "63102442-4ea9-3f8a-b9c8-f864203b25d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a rash manner; hastily or without due consideration; with precipitation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c65d2b1-ee07-4d65-9160-ac7603728592",
                                                "sense_id": "76026db0-b58a-3271-ac62-81e806ed917d",
                                                "text": "Alas Wat, I haue kild the kings officer in ſtriking raſhly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e5b75de-b258-4c55-8184-b7a9511f8276",
                                                "sense_id": "76026db0-b58a-3271-ac62-81e806ed917d",
                                                "text": "VVhy do you ſpeake ſo ſtartingly and raſhly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48569775-bfcb-4071-b68f-7e5c41474d5c",
                                                "sense_id": "76026db0-b58a-3271-ac62-81e806ed917d",
                                                "text": "[H]e'll say that we're contradicting what was said just now when we rashly maintain that there are falsehoods in judgements and statements."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4ac21149-559f-42f0-ac4f-7fda62d576dd",
                        "source_entry_id": "2c32b29e-9aea-3aa2-a5bd-620855b4efa0",
                        "target_lang_word": "recklessly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "recklessly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "541ca3f4-3e33-3cbb-8d67-cd42c410e1d1",
                                        "entry_id": "585cc114-853f-34be-9643-d1225262b5f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a rash or reckless manner, without regard for cost or consequence"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff495713-398d-4bb4-9fc3-dd2e8ea2ed92",
                                                "sense_id": "541ca3f4-3e33-3cbb-8d67-cd42c410e1d1",
                                                "text": "Thanks to that penny he had just spent so recklessly [on a newspaper] he would pass a happy hour, taken, for once, out of his anxious, despondent, miserable self. It irritated him shrewdly to know that these moments of respite from carking care would not be shared with his poor wife, with careworn, troubled Ellen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8879987f-903d-42ff-af52-44d8d49a7338",
                                                "sense_id": "541ca3f4-3e33-3cbb-8d67-cd42c410e1d1",
                                                "text": "Zoe popped her head up to watch in terror through a little window, as they spread chaos and carnage in their wake, not to mention quite a few broken-off wing mirrors. Burt was driving so recklessly, she was frightened he would kill them both."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "874d59e1-c48f-48f8-adf5-37169dc29ce5",
                                                "sense_id": "541ca3f4-3e33-3cbb-8d67-cd42c410e1d1",
                                                "text": "Brooks was also convicted of 61 counts of recklessly endangering safety with the use of a dangerous weapon, six counts of fatal hit and run, two counts of felony bail jumping and one count of misdemeanor domestic battery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40c3e73c-1177-4f92-9533-45282db62fdd",
                                                "sense_id": "541ca3f4-3e33-3cbb-8d67-cd42c410e1d1",
                                                "text": "But some Democrats are raising red flags about DOGE staffers “infiltrating multiple agencies at once,” and “recklessly and haphazardly combining data without any verification or validation,” as one senior House Oversight Committee Democratic staffer put it to CNN."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa0d20ab-5f70-3289-8bbb-1dd5faa8b09f",
                                        "entry_id": "585cc114-853f-34be-9643-d1225262b5f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With contempt for the rights, feelings, or well-being of others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
